// Config for the "Audit dependencies" step in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
//
// Fails CI on any high or critical advisory EXCEPT the ones allowlisted
// below. A plain `npm audit` can't express an exception. The first two
// packages have no patched release (checked 2026-10-15: the advisories
// list no fixed version and the npm registry's latest release of each
// is vulnerable), so an `overrides` pin cannot clear them. The only
// routes `npm audit` suggests are breaking parent changes: a jest 30
// major for braces (jest-expo 57 is on the jest 29 line) and, for
// node-forge, a downgrade from expo-updates 58.0.9 to 0.11.7. Leaving
// them un-allowlisted kept main red and hid any NEW advisory behind the
// same failure.
//
// Remove an entry as soon as its package ships a fix. The audit output
// says "Consider not allowlisting advisory ..." once it is no longer
// vulnerable.
{
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // braces <= 3.0.3: stack-exhaustion DoS on deeply nested patterns.
    // Reached via jest and Metro (micromatch), i.e. test/build tooling.
    "GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm",
    // node-forge <= 1.4.0: RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature verification accepts
    // extra nested DigestAlgorithm elements. Reached via @expo/cli and
    // expo-updates' code-signing certificate tooling.
    "GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv",
    // zod < 4.6.6: memory exhaustion validating oversized constrained
    // collections. Reached via @expo/cli, which pins zod ^3.25.76 (checked
    // 2026-10-26: 57.0.32 is the latest @expo/cli and no 3.x release is
    // patched), so only a zod 4 major would clear it. CLI tooling only.
    "GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5",
  ],
}
